---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import { contactEmail, legal, domain } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using graholskis.com, its content and its resources.">
  <section class="legal-hero">
    <Container>
      <h1 class="h-sec">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="meta legal-updated">Last updated {legal.updated}</p>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <Container as="article" class="legal">
    <p>
      These terms apply to your use of {domain}. The site is run by {legal.owner}, based in {legal.country}.
      By using the site you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Information, not advice</h2>
    <p>
      The articles, cases, diagrams and frameworks on this site are general information based on my experience. They are not legal,
      financial or professional advice for your situation. Consulting work and workshops are always agreed separately in writing,
      and those agreements take priority over these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and reuse</h2>
    <p>
      Unless stated otherwise, the text, diagrams, images and code on this site are my work and protected by copyright.
      You are welcome to link to any page and to quote short passages with a credit and a link back. Please ask before copying whole
      pages or using the diagrams or frameworks in commercial material.
    </p>

    <h2>Paid resources</h2>
    <p>
      Paid resources, such as the blueprint and the online training, are sold through Lemon Squeezy as the merchant of record.
      Lemon Squeezy's terms apply to payment, tax and refunds, and your statutory consumer rights are not affected.
      A purchase gives you a licence for your own use or internal use within your organisation. Reselling or publicly sharing
      the files is not allowed.
    </p>

    <h2>Live tools</h2>
    <p>
      Tools linked from the Labs section, such as Content Factory, are working prototypes. They may change, have limits or be
      unavailable at times. A tool may have its own terms, which apply when you use it.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair use of the site</h2>
    <p>
      Please do not try to break, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site, scrape it at scale, or use the forms to send spam.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      The site links to services I do not control, such as Calendly, LinkedIn, GitHub and YouTube. Their own terms and privacy
      policies apply there, and I am not responsible for their content.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      I keep the site accurate and working, but it is provided "as is" without guarantees. To the extent the law allows, I am not
      liable for indirect or consequential losses from using the site or relying on its content. Nothing in these terms limits
      liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Law and changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of {legal.country}. If you are a consumer, you keep any mandatory protections of the country
      you live in. If the terms change, the new version will be posted here with a new date at the top.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a class="link" href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
